## Experiment design rule (topic isolation)

To keep attribution clean, run each family as a single-topic change while keeping other pillars fixed.

### Family isolation

- Family A (Quality): modify only quality logic.
- Family B (Valuation/Intrinsic): modify only valuation or Reverse DCF logic.
- Family C (Momentum): modify only momentum or timing logic.

### Why this matters

- Clear causality: if results move, we know which pillar caused it.
- Lower interaction noise: avoids false conclusions from mixed parameter changes.
- Faster iteration: easier to keep or discard variants based on robust evidence.

### Two-phase workflow

1. Phase 1: run single-topic families independently and pick the strongest variant in each family.
2. Phase 2: run controlled combinations only after Phase 1 winners are selected:
	- A + B
	- A + C
	- B + C
	- A + B + C
